Damn you Tailscale...





You're just too good. I have spent weeks coding up a project called taildrive (https://github.com/a3l6/taildrive), a distributed file sharing system for your tailnet, combining my love for Tailscale and p2p networks. Then as I'm reading through the docs I see a method named `DriveShareList` so I decide to lookup taildrive....exact same approach to exposing the files. It's not 1:1 but it's close. I try to handle an arbitrary number of protocols, they just use webdav. Theirs is integrated right into tailscale daemon, mine is a separate service.

If you work at tailscale and worked on taildrive, hit me up, I'd love to pick your brain about it.

Man those engineers at tailscale are just too good.....but I probably gotta change the name now.

Check out the signed message:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/a3l6/linkedin-posts/refs/heads/main/taildrive.txt.asc

